cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this harness or its data, please cite it as below."
title: "agent-rules-bench: where should a coding rule live for AI coding agents?"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Çlirim"
    family-names: "Ajeti"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-7976-2785"
repository-code: "https://github.com/clirimajeti/agent-rules-bench"
abstract: >-
  A harness and the data of a controlled benchmark that compares two places
  for the same coding rule for AI coding agents: prose in Markdown instruction
  files (CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md) and lint rules with an in-session feedback loop.
  It holds the study setups, the pre-registered analysis plans, the prompts,
  the transcripts, diffs and logs of every run, the hand labels, and the
  scripts that make every table and number of the paper.
keywords:
  - AI coding agents
  - coding conventions
  - lint rules
  - static analysis
  - context files
  - pre-registration
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
version: "emse-submission"
